# HSM collector conformance v1 — .module start/stop markers (#1433).
# Verbs:
#   add_collector_monitoring_sensors      register the collector-monitoring group under .module:
#                                         Service alive + Collector version + Collector errors.
#                                         C# calls AddCollectorMonitoringSensors on the host's
#                                         collection (the Unix and Windows collections route to one
#                                         implementation; none of the three sensors reads the OS);
#                                         native calls hsm_collector_add_collector_monitoring_sensors.
#   expect_time_marker_comments|prefix|count
#                                         exactly `count` captured payloads carry a comment of the
#                                         form "<prefix>: dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm:ss". A comment that opens
#                                         with "<prefix>: " but loses that shape FAILS, so a broken
#                                         format cannot hide by dropping out of the count. The
#                                         instant itself is wall-clock and is never compared.
# Notes:
# - The heartbeat period is each implementation's own post period (managed: the sensor's
#   PostDataPeriod, 15 s; native: the collector's package-collect period). Every case therefore runs
#   with a 60 s collect period and relies ONLY on the beat that fires immediately on Start; a second
#   beat is provoked by RESTARTING, never by waiting one out. The same long period keeps everything
#   queued until the graceful stop flushes it, so every assertion runs after a stop.
# - `sleep_ms` after each Start is the one wall-clock dependency: the immediate beat is published
#   from a scheduler callback, and a Stop that lands mid-callback legitimately drops it (the managed
#   lifecycle-epoch guard). 300 ms is three orders of magnitude below the 60 s beat period, so the
#   exact counts below stay timing-immune in both directions.
# - The Collector version VALUE is deliberately not asserted: the managed and native collectors are
#   separate products with independent versions (src/native/collector/CLAUDE.md).
# - Payload paths are asserted by SUFFIX ("/Service alive\"") — both drivers prefix the identity.

# Service alive opens a collector's life with `false` (the start marker) — not `true`.
service_alive_first_beat_is_false|create_collector_with_limits|20000|50|60000
service_alive_first_beat_is_false|add_collector_monitoring_sensors
service_alive_first_beat_is_false|start
service_alive_first_beat_is_false|sleep_ms|300
service_alive_first_beat_is_false|stop
service_alive_first_beat_is_false|expect_payload_type_counts|1|0|0|0|0
service_alive_first_beat_is_false|expect_eventually_payload_contains|/Service alive","Value":false,"Status":1,"Comment":""|5

# The start marker is armed once per SENSOR, not once per run: the beat after a restart is `true`.
service_alive_beats_true_after_restart|create_collector_with_limits|20000|50|60000
service_alive_beats_true_after_restart|add_collector_monitoring_sensors
service_alive_beats_true_after_restart|start
service_alive_beats_true_after_restart|sleep_ms|300
service_alive_beats_true_after_restart|stop
service_alive_beats_true_after_restart|start
service_alive_beats_true_after_restart|sleep_ms|300
service_alive_beats_true_after_restart|stop
service_alive_beats_true_after_restart|expect_payload_type_counts|2|0|0|0|0
service_alive_beats_true_after_restart|expect_eventually_payload_contains|/Service alive","Value":false|5
service_alive_beats_true_after_restart|expect_eventually_payload_contains|/Service alive","Value":true|5

# Collector version marks BOTH ends of a run: one "Start:" post and one "Stop:" post, each carrying
# the dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm:ss comment. Three payloads in total: the version twice plus one heartbeat.
collector_version_marks_start_and_stop|create_collector_with_limits|20000|50|60000
collector_version_marks_start_and_stop|add_collector_monitoring_sensors
collector_version_marks_start_and_stop|start
collector_version_marks_start_and_stop|sleep_ms|300
collector_version_marks_start_and_stop|stop
collector_version_marks_start_and_stop|expect_sent_count|3
collector_version_marks_start_and_stop|expect_eventually_payload_contains|/Collector version"|5
collector_version_marks_start_and_stop|expect_time_marker_comments|Start|1
collector_version_marks_start_and_stop|expect_time_marker_comments|Stop|1

# Every run is marked, not just the first: a restart replays the Start/Stop pair.
collector_version_marks_every_run|create_collector_with_limits|20000|50|60000
collector_version_marks_every_run|add_collector_monitoring_sensors
collector_version_marks_every_run|start
collector_version_marks_every_run|sleep_ms|300
collector_version_marks_every_run|stop
collector_version_marks_every_run|start
collector_version_marks_every_run|sleep_ms|300
collector_version_marks_every_run|stop
collector_version_marks_every_run|expect_sent_count|6
collector_version_marks_every_run|expect_time_marker_comments|Start|2
collector_version_marks_every_run|expect_time_marker_comments|Stop|2

# The group registers exactly its three sensors, once per start.
collector_monitoring_group_registers_three|create_collector_with_limits|20000|50|60000
collector_monitoring_group_registers_three|add_collector_monitoring_sensors
collector_monitoring_group_registers_three|start
collector_monitoring_group_registers_three|stop
collector_monitoring_group_registers_three|expect_registration_count|3
